# Database And Migrations

Shared ecosystem schema lives in `supabase/migrations/**`. App schemas (for example XFlow Drizzle) live inside nested app repos.

Never let Cursor and Codex create competing migrations in parallel. Schema work is serialized unless the user explicitly coordinates ordering.

## Before any schema change

1. Inspect current schema and existing migrations
2. Confirm ordering and forward-only history
3. Identify backwards compatibility and rollback implications
4. Checkpoint before applying

Do not rewrite applied migrations. Do not modify production data as part of ordinary development. Do not run destructive reset/seed scripts unless the user names that operation and the target is clearly non-production.

Worktree setup must not auto-migrate. Apply migrations only as an explicit, in-scope step of the task.
